{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_usage_pins_export_import_pin", "label": "Pin", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/usage/pins-export-import.md", "source_location": "docs/usage/pins-export-import.md#pinning-packages", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Supports three pin kinds: Pinning (excluded from bulk upgrade-all, explicit upgrade still allowed), Gating (only upgrades matching a version pattern such as 2.44.*), and Blocking (no upgrade until the pin is removed)."}, {"id": "docs_usage_pins_export_import_getpins", "label": "GetPins", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/usage/pins-export-import.md", "source_location": "docs/usage/pins-export-import.md#pinning-packages", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CLI-backed; its results come from parsing `winget pin list` output because no COM equivalent exists."}, {"id": "docs_usage_pins_export_import_unpin", "label": "Unpin", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/usage/pins-export-import.md", "source_location": "docs/usage/pins-export-import.md#pinning-packages", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_usage_pins_export_import_export", "label": "Export", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/usage/pins-export-import.md", "source_location": "docs/usage/pins-export-import.md#export", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Snapshots installed packages to a winget import-compatible JSON file; a non-zero exit still writes the file for everything it could map, so existence of the file is the practical success check."}, {"id": "docs_usage_pins_export_import_import", "label": "Import", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/usage/pins-export-import.md", "source_location": "docs/usage/pins-export-import.md#import", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Installs everything an exported file lists, with ignoreUnavailable to skip packages no longer in any source and ignoreVersions to choose whether exported versions are honored."}, {"id": "docs_usage_pins_export_import_clioperationresult", "label": "CliOperationResult", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/usage/pins-export-import.md", "source_location": "docs/usage/pins-export-import.md#cli-results", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Because there is no structured COM result for CLI-backed operations, it captures the process outcome directly: Succeeded (ExitCode == 0), ExitCode/ExitCodeHex whose hex form matches WinGet's documented APPINSTALLER_CLI_ERROR_* HRESULTs, and captured stdout/stderr."}, {"id": "docs_usage_pins_export_import_winget_exe_resolution", "label": "winget.exe resolution strategy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/usage/pins-export-import.md", "source_location": "docs/usage/pins-export-import.md#how-wingetexe-is-located", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resolves the per-user App Execution Alias first, then globs the WindowsApps package directory and picks the highest version \u2014 the strategy enterprise deployments such as Winget-AutoUpdate use, which matters because service/SYSTEM contexts have no App Execution Alias. If neither works, WinGetUnavailableException is thrown."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_usage_pins_export_import_pin", "target": "docs_architecture_iwingetcliclient", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/usage/pins-export-import.md", "source_location": "docs/usage/pins-export-import.md#pins-export--import", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_usage_pins_export_import_export", "target": "docs_architecture_iwingetcliclient", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file":